From 889ade9e225d83756d22208a7c68186b9ec466e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 07:24:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(rust-rounds): a work span starts no earlier than the last
 one closed (RR26)

One span open at a time held by the order events reached home, not by
their instants: the phone can keep a start offline that home would have
refused and send it after another span has closed, and home kept it, so
two spans overlapped in time and counted twice.

work_span::start now refuses a start whose `at` is before the subject's
latest close `at`, compared as instants (crate::instant_order), whatever
their offsets; one exactly at it is kept. The latest close is the newest
start's, read in the same indexed step as the open span (`newest`, which
`open` now filters). The held-span check still comes first, so a retry of
a start home keeps answers 200 unchanged even after a later span closed.

The refusal is a 409 (SpanError::Overlaps, SPAN_OVERLAPS) in the plain
error envelope: the start is valid by itself and conflicts with another
span home holds, like a start while one is open, and no retry can succeed.
No response shape changes, so no epoch moves.

Also: the raw-SQL trigger test asserts each refusal's message, and the
docs say idempotency compares `at` as text, since the phone re-sends its
stored string byte for byte. The first test's second span now starts
after the first closed, as it overlapped it.

